  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following species exhibits the diamagnetic behaviour?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WB3TY",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2^{2-}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "j9I5v",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ajJgC",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "04J9n",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{NO}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The correct option is $\\mathrm{O}_2^{2-}$\nThis species has $18 \\mathrm{~e}^{-}$, which are filled in such a way that all molecular orbitals are fully filled, so diamagnetic.\n$\\mathrm{\\sigma 1 s^2 \\sigma^* 1 s^2, \\sigma 2 s^2 \\sigma^* 2 s^2, \\sigma 2 p_z^2, \\pi 2 p_x^2=\\pi 2 p_y^2, \\pi^* 2 p_x^2=\\pi^* 2 p_y^2}$\nHence, (A) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
